From bc5da6aa5371fcb0327da2ff857cbfddffa4403c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:11:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: resolve a collapsed table's borders
 line by line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A border-collapse: collapse table was laid out with one uniform gutter, as
wide as its first cell's widest border, and painted in that cell's colour.
Every other cell's border, and every row's, row group's and column's, was
ignored: a row's border-bottom drew nothing and took no room.

collapse_borders resolves each segment of each line between grid slots, and
around the grid, from the borders of the cells, rows, row groups, columns,
column groups and the table that meet there (CSS 2.2 §17.6.2.1): hidden
wins, then the wider, the higher-priority style and the higher-ranked box.
Each cell's border is half of the widest segment on each of its sides, the
table's half of its widest outer line, and the table has no padding, as in
Chromium. Cells read their border through TaffyStyloStyle::collapsed_border,
and a cell whose lines change has its layout cache cleared. The table paints
each segment centred on the cells' edge, from their painted layouts, one
fill per colour; a cell paints its background in its padding box and no
border, and the table none of its own. Columns run in the table's direction.
This replaces the gutter painting and PhysicalTracks.

The column cursor freed a rowspan cell's columns one row early, so the cell
beside it in its second row was given the wrong column. It now counts the
current row.
